From ac1cf05f22309d03f7292cb91aa1513615c753bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 16:09:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Add Incomplete outcome: variant, rendering, and TODO:
 detection

Introduce a third test outcome alongside Ok/Fail/Skip:

- `Incomplete of string variant in Run_result.t
- is_failure: false (does not affect exit code)
- has_run: true (appears in "N tests run" summary)
- [INCOMPLETE] tag in yellow, compact char 'I'
- protect_test catches Failure whose message starts with "TODO:"
  and routes it to `Incomplete

Tests that call failwith "TODO: reason" are marked [INCOMPLETE]
instead of [FAIL]. When no test raises such a failure, all new
branches are unreachable and upstream behaviour is unchanged.
