Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Render [INCOMPLETE] breakdown below verdict line

When the Incomplete message carries multi-line content, render the
lines after the first indented under the verdict name column
(16 spaces = left_gutter + left_tag).

The lines are wrapped in an explicit @[<v>...@] vbox so @, acts as a
hard cut instead of being packed together by Format's default margin.

Single-line messages (e.g. failwith "TODO: not yet implemented") hit
the no-render branch and are visually unchanged.

New regression test incomplete_breakdown_in_test exercises the
multi-line path. Its .expected file pins the exact column layout;
the existing incomplete_in_test.expected continues to pass unchanged.
