From 664925b944b2ee69c36da28e7ccb06ec015cd6c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Sat, 2 May 2026 19:52:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Remove set_test_suffix from the incomplete-PBT patch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

set_test_suffix was added to let the QCheck alcotest adapter append a
pass/incomplete/failed stats summary to each test's verdict line in the
alcotest output.  After review we decided to drop it:

- It is purely cosmetic (the counts are not needed for the [INCOMPLETE]
  verdict, which is driven entirely by the failwith "TODO:..." convention).
- It extends the public interface of alcotest (test.mli) and the internal
  Pp contract (pp_intf.ml), making the patch larger and harder to upstream.
- The QCheck adapter (QCheck_alcotest.ml) can report the same information
  via stdout printf before raising, without touching alcotest's API.

The [INCOMPLETE] outcome, its printer, the protect_test arm, and the e2e
regression test are all preserved — only the suffix machinery is removed.

